  "steps": [
    "Heat the oven to 350°F.",
    "In a large (12 in) oven-safe skillet over high heat, combine the strawberries, brown sugar, cornstarch and 3 tbsp butter. Boil 5-10 min, until the juices bubble and turn jammy. Off the heat, stir in the vanilla.",
    "In a bowl, whisk the melted butter, brown sugar, egg and vanilla. Stir in the flour, oats, baking soda and salt.",
    "Drop the cookie dough in clumps over the fruit. Bake 30 min.",
    "Take the skillet out, dot the 4 tbsp butter over the top, and drizzle with the maple syrup or honey. Bake 15 min more, until the topping is golden and the fruit bubbles at the edges.",
    "Cool 10 min and serve warm with whipped cream or ice cream."
  ],
  "tips": [
    "No oven-safe skillet? Cook the fruit in any pan and move it to a baking dish before topping.",
    "Tieghan uses the smaller amount of brown sugar in both the berries and the topping.",
    "Can be assembled ahead and refrigerated. Bring to room temp before baking.",
    "Works with mixed berries or peaches, and with gluten-free flour and oats."
  ],
